# Secrets and local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.postgres.example
**/.dlt/secrets.toml
*.p8
*.pem

# Ad-hoc SQL scratch at the repository root. These are where a credential actually
# gets typed: `ALTER SECRET ... SET SECRET_STRING = '<key>'` has to be run by hand
# once per secret, and the file it was typed into then sits in the working tree as
# an ordinary untracked file that `git add .` would happily stage.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING, as it is for /.docs/ below. These patterns must
# match only the repository root: dlt-pipelines/sql/ and dbt-pipelines/ are full of
# committed .sql, and a bare `test.sql` or `scratch*.sql` would match at any depth.
/test.sql
/scratch.sql
/scratch*.sql

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# dlt
duck-db/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
.dlt/pipelines/
build/

# dbt
target/
dbt_packages/
logs/

# Node (docs sites)
node_modules/
dist/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
*.swp

# Agent session state and working artifacts.
# .snowflake/ is where Cortex Code writes its plans; they are scratch for one
# session, not a record of the project. The two PLAN files are closed-out session
# logs kept on disk deliberately -- the runbooks (MAKE-COMMANDS-*.md) are what an
# adopter actually needs and those ARE committed.
.snowflake/
.claude/settings.local.json
logs.txt

# Reference material kept locally, not redistributed. Holds the BallDontLie
# OpenAPI specs, which are the provider's to publish rather than ours, plus
# working notes. Nothing in the build reads from here.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING: it anchors this to the repository root. A bare
# `.docs/` matches at any depth and would also swallow dlt-pipelines/.docs/,
# which is vendored dlt reference that its README documents and links to.
/.docs/
FIX-PLAN.md
FIX-PLAN.html
SPCS-PLAN.md

# Session records and the personal task tracker: working notes for the
# maintainer, not part of the public codebase. They stay on disk (CLAUDE.md
# and the session tooling read them) but are not published.
WORKFLOW-*.md
BACKLOG.md
BACKLOG.html
OBS-LINEAGE.html

# Vendor reference downloads at the repository root (e.g. Snowflake's Credit
# Consumption Table PDF): theirs to publish, ours to read locally. Leading
# slash anchors to the root, same as /.docs/ above.
/*.pdf

# Local working copy of an upstream template: reference material for the
# maintainer, never part of this codebase.
/dlt-snowflake-template/

# Build guide for porting the ops layer into the template repo: written here,
# consumed elsewhere. Not part of this codebase.
/OPS-PORT.md
.brainstorm/

# Generated from env (passwords). Applied by make setup-postgres /
# setup-postgres-secret; never commit.
**/.generated/
